<title>USA: W. Virginia jobless rate rises to 6.3 pct in July.</title>
<headline>W. Virginia jobless rate rises to 6.3 pct in July.</headline>
<dateline>CHARLESTON, W.Va. 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>West Virginia's unemployment rate edged up to 6.3 percent in July from 6.2 percent in June, the state Bureau of Employment Programs said.</p>
<p>Despite the increase, the July unemployment rate was the lowest for the month since 1978. About 2,000 West Virginia residents lost their jobs during the month, putting the unemployment total at 52,000 residents.</p>
<p>((--Jane Sutton, 305-374-5013))</p>
</text>
